GOAL
Create ONE new page: "Expense Hub". It shows all expenses from all modules in
one place. On this page, Finance decides for each expense whether VAT applies.
The page must connect directly to our existing VAT format/report.

STRICT RULES (most important)
1. DO NOT change, rename, or delete any existing table, column, model,
   controller, page, route, or SMS/notification logic.
2. READ-ONLY on all existing tables. Never write to them from the Hub.
3. All new data goes in NEW tables only (prefix: expense_hub_).
4. If something existing must be touched, STOP and ask me first.

WHAT THE HUB SHOWS
- Count only actual paid money, once (cash basis). No double counting.
- Sources: procurement_payments, credit_store_payments, expense_requests (paid),
  petty_cash_material_purchases, payrolls, employee_advances, ipc_records
  (paid), tax_settlements, fixed_assets (as separate CapEx category).
- Do NOT count: purchase_requests, proformas, receipts, budgets, journal
  entries (these are estimates or proof only).
- Petty cash replenishment is a fund transfer, not an expense.
- Each row: date, source module, source ID (link to the original record),
  project/site, payee/supplier, TIN, amount, payment method, paid by,
  receipt link, VAT status.

VAT DECISION (core feature)
- Each row has a VAT status: "VAT applies", "No VAT", or "Pending decision".
- Default by source, based on what the source already has:
  * If the source already has vat_amount > 0 -> "VAT applies" (prefilled)
  * If vat_amount is empty/0 -> "Pending decision"
  * Payroll, salary advances, tax settlements -> "No VAT" by default
- Finance can change the status per row, and in bulk (select many rows).
- When "VAT applies" and the source has no VAT amount, calculate it with a
  configurable rate (default 15%) and let the user choose whether the entered
  amount is VAT-inclusive or VAT-exclusive. Show base, VAT, and total.
- When "No VAT", require a short reason (dropdown + note), e.g. no TIN on
  receipt, exempt item, salary, informal vendor.
- Warn (do not block) if "VAT applies" but there is no vendor TIN or no
  fiscal receipt.
- Save all decisions in new tables: expense_hub_vat_decisions
  (source_type, source_id, vat_status, vat_rate, vat_amount, base_amount,
  reason, decided_by, decided_at). Keep a full history of changes (audit log).
- Lock a decision after the month is closed, unless the Finance Head unlocks it.

